request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (The request renames the shared Todo.done field to Todo.completed. types owns the definition, and format, storage, and commands all consume Todo, so all four are targeted with one exact new interface as the contract. The compiler plus per-unit acceptance tests will catch any missed reference.)
round 1: owners types=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (All four round-1 rejections were purely mechanical `done` → `completed` renames in existing test data, which the request requires (the old key would not compile against the new Todo type). Approving those four test changes and re-issuing the same rename plan; acceptance tests pinning the new field name stay in place.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The Todo.done → Todo.completed rename is fully applied: types exports the new Todo shape, and commands, format, and storage all re-keyed to `completed`. Oracle is GREEN (tsc clean, 17/17 tests pass), and acceptance tests confirm completed-only Todos, the "completed" JSON key on disk with no "done" residue, and correct completion behaviour through commands.)

